  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowering Vulnerable Children Affected by the Earthquake in North-West Syria through Individual Protection Assistance (IPA).</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to address the unmet protection needs of children profoundly impacted by the earthquake. Post-earthquake, Child Houses (CH) witnessed a notable increase in the number of vulnerable children. The project aims to specifically target these affected children by providing Individual Protection Assistance (IPA), a direct and time-sensitive intervention crafted to achieve distinct protection goals and strengthen the child&#x2019;s resilience, development, and safety.</narrative>
  </description>
